  "preamble": "Loanword adaptation of the voiceless postalveolar affricate [tʃ] as the voiceless alveolo-palatal affricate [tɕ]. Japanese has no postalveolar affricate; English /tʃ/ is borrowed with the kana チ/チャ/チュ/チェ/チョ, whose consonant is the alveolo-palatal [tɕ] (historically the palatalized allophone of /t/).",
